  "scope": "Windows/Linux each pass 22 native suites (21 CTest plus one owned native batch suite), three full C++ workflow/batch/RGB UI probes, ten background repetitions, four hidden background GL contexts and 3793 installed Python checks, zero failure/error/skip. Seventy-one new Python cases cover saved and authored mapping, complete historical validation before override, all target scopes across scalar UInt8/UInt16 with whole/active/positioned ROIs, observed/configured reset ranges, threshold clearing and LUT retention, ordered histogram outputs, scaled conversion using the actual preceding reset range, paired history and stale publication. They cover invalid/disabled portable intent before source reads, cancellation/callback failure, common/per-input Batch setup codecs, selected/all session documents, unchanged inputs/session tables, staged versus final files and failure before publication. Expanded native fixtures verify sample-blocking admission descriptors, malformed later steps without provider reads, mid-kernel cancellation, independent pixels and actual workflow mapping fields including invalid numeric correction, Prepare and Apply. Linux builds and installed tests use byte-verified native filesystem source/test snapshots. Final origins map to retained qualified installs and probes; scratch is CRC/member-SHA verified before exact owned removal. All original 99 requirement/status triples and existing build/test registrations are preserved. This is scoped scalar Apply workflow/batch integration, not full ImageJ/Fiji/G057 or resource/platform acceptance.",
